---
/**
 * NavProgressBar — thin brand-yellow bar fixed at the very top of the page
 * (navigation-without-flicker PR). All the actual behavior (when it
 * appears, how it trickles, when it completes/aborts) lives in
 * `src/lib/navProgress.ts`'s `NavProgressController` + `initNavProgressBar`
 * — this file is markup plus the one call that wires them to real
 * `document` events.
 *
 * `transition:persist`: the SAME reasoning as `Header.astro` — this element
 * (and the module script below, which only ever runs once regardless) must
 * survive every client-side navigation rather than being swapped for a
 * fresh, unstyled copy.
 *
 * `width`/`opacity` are driven entirely from JS (`applyNavProgressState`);
 * the inline `style` below is only the pre-JS/no-JS resting state (hidden).
 * `transition: opacity` (not `width`) is the only animated CSS property —
 * the trickle's own width JUMPS are the animation for `active`/`completing`
 * (matches the controller's discrete ticks); only the fade OUT should ease.
 * `motion-reduce:` disables even that, per the task's reduced-motion
 * requirement (appear/disappear only, no animation).
 */
---

<div
  id="nav-progress-bar"
  data-testid="nav-progress-bar"
  aria-hidden="true"
  transition:persist
  transition:animate="none"
  class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-50 h-[3px] bg-primary opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 ease-out motion-reduce:transition-none"
  style="width:0%"
>
</div>

<script>
  import { initNavProgressBar } from '@lib/navProgress';
  initNavProgressBar();
</script>
